    report += [table(['Civil occurrence','Sizing driver','Gross floor area m²','Enclosed air m³','Civil cost $M'],[(n,driver(n),num(baseline[L+n+'_gross_area']),num(baseline[L+n+'_air_volume']),num(baseline[B+n+'__civil__cost_2025']/1e6)) for n in civilnames]),'',f'Total civil cost is ${num(baseline[CIV]/1e6)} million; nuclear ventilation adds ${num(baseline[B+"ventilation__cost_2025"]/1e6)} million. The retained site allowance is ${num(baseline[B+"site_allowance__cost"]/1e6)} million. The installed facility subtotal eligible for the facility shipping exclusion is ${num(baseline[INST]/1e6)} million; it excludes that retained site allowance. The actual contingency-loaded facility shipping exclusion is ${num(baseline[P+"shipping_scope__facility_exclusion"]/1e6)} million. Selected default14 preconstruction capital changes from ${num(byid["default14-legacy"][P+"facility_preconstruction__cost"]/1e6)} to ${num(baseline[P+"facility_preconstruction__cost"]/1e6)} million with the new land requirement.','', 'The sector wings represent hot-cell functions: controlled spaces intended for remote work on radioactive components. Remote handling means moving and servicing those components without direct human access. The reactor hall and four sector wings follow the reactor exterior envelope, withdrawal space, access corridors and maintenance stock. The cooling hall follows circuit count, exchanger pull space and machine envelopes; its annex follows dated receipt, waiting, processing and storage demand. Ten support-equipment rooms use explicit provisional envelopes; three support rooms use occupancy assumptions. Fuel construction uses the nuclear scenario. Dimensions of these conventional-support functions are not presented as calculated equipment designs.']
    if (R/'baseline-layout.svg').exists():report += ['', '![Calculated conceptual site footprints](results/baseline-layout.svg)']
    report += ['', '## Response to equipment dimensions', '', table(['Case','Major radius m','Minor radius m','Circuits','Gross building area m²','Installed facility subtotal $M','LCOE $/MWh'],[(r['proposal_id'],num(r['input:'+P+'plasma__R']),num(r['input:'+P+'plasma__a']),int(r['input:'+P+'heat_transport__n_loops']),num(r[L+'total_gross_area']),num(r[INST]/1e6),num(r[LC],3)) for r in rows if r['family']=='equipment-response' or r['proposal_id']=='default14-layout']), '', 'These equipment-response cases vary one declared input from default14. They rerun the existing plant physics and maintenance calendar, rather than holding computed duties or component demand artificially fixed. They are distinct from the selected18 retained-context comparison, where several plant inputs differ together.']
    report += ['', '## Maintenance capacity and conflicts','',f'The default case requires {int(baseline[L+"packages_per_sector"])} packages per sector, {int(baseline[L+"dirty_buffer_required"])} waiting positions and {int(baseline[L+"dirty_store_required"])} finished-waste positions per wing. The assumed intervention takes {num(baseline[L+"outage_required_days"])} days against {num(baseline[L+"outage_allowed_days"])} offered. Initial readiness has {num(baseline[L+"initial_margin_days"])} days of margin; recurring batch readiness has {num(baseline[L+"readiness_margin_days"])}. These margins include completion of initial cooling carrier returns before commissioning.','',f'{len(failrows)} of {len(rows)} cases fail at least one facility screen. The table retains all such cases; negative values indicate the particular schedule, capacity or route conflict.','',table(['Case','Initial days','Recurring days','Outage days','Stock/resource count','Route/site metres','Failed facility screens'],[(r['proposal_id'],num(r[L+'initial_margin_days']),num(r[L+'readiness_margin_days']),num(r[L+'outage_margin_days']),num(r[L+'capacity_margin_units']),num(r[L+'route_margin_m']),', '.join(failed(r,facility))) for r in failrows]),'', 'Resized storage adds space when stock grows; it does not create more crew time, move a nominal delivery deadline or make an oversized package fit a 6m door. The fixed/resized hold and processing pairs preserve that distinction. Zero recurring replacement cases still include initial demand. The changed fluence-limit case is a zero-event branch diagnostic; the reference maintenance requirement remains unchanged. A positive horizon-length outage margin in a zero-event case is a satisfied sentinel, not extra outage time or demonstrated intervention capacity. The model does not silently change availability to repair a facility conflict. Detailed inventories and serialized carrier/service reservations are retained in the per-case facility ledgers.']
    slow=byid['tasks-0.75'];hold=byid['sector-hold6-mode1']
    report += ['', f'Slower0.75-day removal/install tasks reduce the dirty waiting peak to {int(slow[L+"dirty_buffer_required"])} positions and gross area to {num(slow[L+"total_gross_area"])}m². LCOE falls to {num(slow[LC],6)}, but the outage margin is {num(slow[L+"outage_margin_days"],4)} days: the lower cost belongs to a failed schedule. Six-year sector storage requires {int(hold[L+"dirty_store_required"])} finished positions per wing versus {int(baseline[L+"dirty_store_required"])} initially; resizing expands gross area to {num(hold[L+"total_gross_area"])}m² and LCOE to {num(hold[LC],6)}.']
